            "review_title": "Review at Cookie's House",
            "review_text": "DeltaBeta\nMelbourne, Australia6 contributions\n0\nAmazing drinks and cakes\nDec 2016 • Couples\nTucked away, this place offers a great spot to cool down (literally) in a relaxing, ambient environment. The menu is written in full english, is easy to navigate and includes prices. The waitstaff are friendly and the service is prompt. Another bonus is that it comes with complimentary iced tea while you wait for your order. \n\nFor the drinks I tried both the Purple Monkey and the Bubblegum Milk. Both were amazing, an unlike anything I have tried back in Australia. Sweet, cold and creamy; they hit just the right spot after an afternoon facing the heat and humidity of Ho Chi Minh.\n\nWhile drinks are the main attraction, they do offer a few selections of food. I tried and would highly recommend the Fried Sweet Corn. Battered corn comes served with a spicy chilli dipping sauce and tasted great! \n\nOverall this is a really great place to just kick back, relax and enjoy a cool drink. Anybody who has had a long day burning the pavement of HCM should reward themselves with a trip here!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 22, 2016",
